@startuml accounts-login-and-session-sequence
!include ../../_style/sequence.iuml
title Accounts > Login and session — sign in, who is signed in, each request, sign out

actor Reader
participant "LoginPage\n+ AuthProvider" as Client
participant "loginRouter\n+ rateLimit" as Router
participant loginController as Controller
participant loginService as Service
participant "pwdHasher\n(bcrypt)" as Hasher
participant jwt as Jwt
participant "sessionRouter" as Session
participant "passwordChanges\n+ admin" as Checks
participant "loginModel\n+ userModel" as Model
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Sign in ==
Reader -> Client : username, password
Client -> Client : both filled, else "This field is required"
Client -> Router : POST /api/login {username, password}
alt more than 10 tries from this address in 15 minutes
    Router --> Client : 429 {error, retryAfter}
end
Router -> Controller : authUser(req)
alt a field missing or not a string
    Controller --> Client : 400
end
Controller -> Service : authUser({username, password})
Service -> Model : getUserByUsername(username)
Model -> DB : SELECT users WHERE username, whatever its case\n(the exact name first)
Service -> Hasher : verifyPassword(password,\nits hash or NO_ACCOUNT)
note right of Hasher : an unknown name costs\nthe same bcrypt (cost 12)
alt no such user, or a wrong password
    Service --> Client : 401 "Invalid username or password..."
end
Service -> Jwt : generateAccessToken({id, username, email, role})
Service --> Controller : {id_user, token}
Controller -> Jwt : startSession(res, token)
note right of Jwt : Set-Cookie session: HttpOnly,\nSameSite=Strict, path /api,\nSecure in https, 7 days
Controller --> Client : 200 {id_user}, never the token

== Who is signed in ==
Client -> Session : GET /api/session (the cookie)
Session -> Jwt : authenticateToken
Jwt -> Checks : passwordChangedAt(id)
opt not known yet in this process
    Checks -> Model : passwordChangedAt(id)
    Model -> DB : SELECT users.password_changed_at
end
alt no cookie, a bad or expired token
    Jwt --> Client : 403 "Forbidden, invalid or expired token..."
else account gone, or token older than the last change of password
    Jwt --> Client : 403
else the check fails (the database)
    Jwt --> Client : 503
end
opt token older than 24 h
    Jwt -> Jwt : startSession(new token): 7 days again
end
par
    Session -> Model : email(id): username, email now
else
    Session -> Checks : isAdmin(id)
    Checks -> Model : roleName(id)
    Model -> DB : users JOIN roles
end
Session --> Client : 200 {id, username, email, role, admin}
Client --> Reader : the briefing; the masthead with the name

== Any other route ==
note over Client, DB
    Open without a session: /login, /signup, DELETE /session, GET /news/categories, GET /profile/options,
    the profile funnel while SIGNUP_OPEN=1, GET /mails/:token. Every other route runs authenticateToken
    first, the same checks, then activeProfile (header X-Profile). useAuth.expired() sends the reader to
    the login when an answer says "Forbidden, invalid or expired". adminOnly(): 403 for the e-mail of the
    briefing, its pictures and a news added by its link; a second profile is refused by ProfileService.
end note

== Sign out ==
Reader -> Client : Sign out
Client -> Client : forget(): user null, forgetSearch(),\nsetActiveProfile(null)
Client -> Session : DELETE /api/session
Session -> Jwt : endSession(res)
Session --> Client : 204, the cookie cleared
@enduml
